{"subjectId":"javascript","id":"control-flow","title":"Control Flow & Loops","group":"Types, Values & Operators","order":12,"html":"<p class=\"lead\"><code>if</code>/<code>else</code>, <code>switch</code>, the ternary, five kinds of loop, and <code>break</code>/<code>continue</code> with labels.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-arrows-split-2\"></i>Conditionals</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const grade = (score) =&gt; {\n  if (score &gt;= 90) return \"A\";\n  else if (score &gt;= 75) return \"B\";\n  else return \"C\";\n};\nconsole.log(grade(95), grade(80), grade(10));\nconst age = 20;\nconsole.log(age &gt;= 18 ? \"adult\" : \"minor\");</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>A B C\nadult</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-switch\"></i><code>switch</code> uses strict equality and falls through</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>function kind(day) {\n  switch (day) {\n    case \"sat\":\n    case \"sun\":\n      return \"weekend\";\n    case 1:\n      return \"number one\";\n    default:\n      return \"weekday\";\n  }\n}\nconsole.log(kind(\"sun\"), kind(\"mon\"), kind(1), kind(\"1\"));\n\nlet log = [];\nswitch (2) {\n  case 1: log.push(1);\n  case 2: log.push(2);   // no break → falls through\n  case 3: log.push(3);\n    break;\n  case 4: log.push(4);\n}\nconsole.log(log);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>weekend weekday number one weekday\n[ 2, 3 ]</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-repeat\"></i>Loops</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Loop</th><th>Iterates over</th><th>Use for</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>for (init; cond; step)</code></td><td>a counter</td><td>index-based work, early exit</td></tr><tr><td><code>while (cond)</code></td><td>until the condition fails</td><td>unknown number of iterations</td></tr><tr><td><code>do { } while (cond)</code></td><td>at least once</td><td>prompts / retries</td></tr><tr><td><code>for (const x of iterable)</code></td><td><strong>values</strong> of arrays, strings, maps, sets, generators</td><td>the default for arrays</td></tr><tr><td><code>for (const k in object)</code></td><td>enumerable <strong>keys</strong> (incl. inherited) as strings</td><td>plain objects only</td></tr><tr><td><code>arr.forEach(fn)</code></td><td>array elements</td><td>side effects; cannot <code>break</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const arr = [\"a\", \"b\"];\narr.extra = \"!\";\nfor (const i in arr) console.log(\"in:\", i, typeof i);\nfor (const v of arr) console.log(\"of:\", v);\nfor (const [i, v] of arr.entries()) console.log(i, v);\nfor (const ch of \"hi\") console.log(ch);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>in: 0 string\nin: 1 string\nin: extra string\nof: a\nof: b\n0 a\n1 b\nh\ni</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--warn\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Watch out</div><p>Never use <code>for…in</code> on arrays: keys are strings, order is not guaranteed by intent, and it also visits extra/inherited enumerable properties. Use <code>for…of</code>.</p></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-rotate\"></i>while / do…while</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>let n = 1;\nwhile (n &lt; 100) n *= 3;\nconsole.log(n);\nlet tries = 0;\ndo {\n  tries++;\n} while (false);\nconsole.log(tries);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>243\n1</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-player-skip-forward\"></i>break, continue and labels</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>for (let i = 0; i &lt; 6; i++) {\n  if (i === 1) continue;\n  if (i === 4) break;\n  console.log(i);\n}\nouter: for (let r = 0; r &lt; 3; r++) {\n  for (let c = 0; c &lt; 3; c++) {\n    if (c === 1) continue outer;\n    if (r === 2) break outer;\n    console.log(`r${r}c${c}`);\n  }\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>0\n2\n3\nr0c0\nr1c0</code></pre></figure>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>What is the difference between for...in and for...of?</summary><div><p><code>for…in</code> iterates over the enumerable <em>property keys</em> (strings) of an object, including inherited ones. <code>for…of</code> iterates over the <em>values</em> produced by an iterable (arrays, strings, Map, Set, generators). Use <code>for…of</code> for arrays and <code>Object.entries(obj)</code> with <code>for…of</code> for objects.</p></div></details>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>Can you break out of forEach?</summary><div><p>No — <code>break</code> is a syntax error inside the callback and <code>return</code> only skips to the next element. Use <code>for…of</code>, or <code>some</code>/<code>every</code>/<code>find</code>, which stop early.</p></div></details></section>"}